 "strategy": "Names. The largest failure class is NameError: the body uses names that the signature does not have (it writes a habitual name such as `n`, `numbers` or `s` where the argument is called something else). Find what makes the model prefer its habitual names over the names of the prompt, and change it. Candidates: (a) feed-forward units of the last layer whose W2 column points along the E rows of the habitual name tokens (they push those names; scale such columns down); (b) the attention heads that copy from the signature: find with a trace of `l<k>.e` the query head whose weights at body positions sit on the argument tokens, and strengthen what it writes (scale its columns of Wo up, as far as int8 allows), or sharpen it through its score offset c_s or the EXP table of its layer; (c) the E rows of the habitual name tokens themselves (E is input and output at once, so be careful).",
